# Paper material: local-only, never published.
#
# Everything under papers/ derives from someone else's paper: the figure crops are verbatim
# extracts from the source PDF, the content is a translation (a derivative work) of the original
# text, and the manifests carry the papers' identity and section maps. None of it is covered by
# LICENSE, so it stays out of the public repository. The pipeline regenerates the figures from a
# PDF you supply yourself, and `git ls-files papers` must stay empty.
papers/

# The LLM survey: local-only, never published.
#
# survey/ holds original survey prose plus translations of the surveyed papers' abstracts. The
# prose is ours, but the abstracts are derivative works of the papers themselves, and the two are
# interleaved in the same files, so the whole tree stays out of the published repository - the
# same reasoning that keeps papers/ untracked. Build the deliverable with tools/survey.py.
#
# Anchored to the repository root on purpose: a bare `survey/` would also match the tracked
# source directory `src/survey/`, silently dropping the survey stylesheet from the repository.
/survey/

# Local-only and generated content
.tasks/
.local/
.logs/
.reports/
.tmp/
.pi/
dist/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/

# Node (tooling only)
node_modules/

# Editors and OS noise
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Secrets
.env
.env.*
